                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game looks really outdated, and the training mechanics are just annoying. The building upgrades look like they're from 1990.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1780767513,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1780767513,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 1,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.43478259444236755,
                        "comment_count": 1,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hello,\n\nI'm sorry you didn't enjoy my game.\n\nAbout the visuals and the building upgrades : they are clearly shown on the Steam store page, so if they were a deal-breaker for you, the store page should have made that clear before buying, shouldn’t it ? 🤔\n\nAbout the training mechanics : did you try using the Training Schedules ? They are meant to avoid having to manually repeat the same training setup again and again.\n\nIt seems you got a refund, which is good if you didn't want to play the game anymore. But if the visuals were the main issue, and as they were already visible before buying, would you consider removing your review ? Thanks for giving some thought about that. 🙂\n\nAnd if the training part was the main issue, feel free to let me know if you tried the Training Schedules or not, because maybe I can help you with that.\n",
